    "https://clarku.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204449": {
      "title": "Clark University \n\tJob Posting: Electronic Resource Acquisitions Librarian",
      "description": "Clark University\nJob Posting: Electronic Resource Acquisitions Librarian Clark University \n\tJob Posting: Electronic Resource Acquisitions Librarian Title Home Human Resources Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Electronic Resource Acquisitions Librarian Category: Staff and Administrators Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: LIBR-Goddard Library 2122 Locations: Worcester, MA Posted: Sep 3, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time - Exempt Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $51,700.00 - $68,150.00 Position ID: 204449 Share About Clark University: Founded in 1887, Clark was one of the first all-graduate institutions in the United States. Today the University is a highly-ranked, student-centered institution educating approximately 2,350 undergraduate and 1,150 graduate students to be imaginative and contributing citizens of the world and to advance the frontiers of knowledge and understanding through rigorous scholarship and creative effort. This commitment to scholarship and inquiry reflects the University's commitment to \"challenge convention and change our world\" and to address issues of critical importance to society. It is also reflected by Clark's many national and international distinctions, including innovation, community engagement and impact, as a top green campus, and for having a distinguished geography and international development program. Clark has also been included in the groundbreaking Colleges that Change Lives guide since it was first published in 1996. Clark is located in Worcester, Massachusetts, a dynamic, diverse city \"on the rise\". The second largest city in New England, Worcester is home to 11 institutions of higher learning and is increasingly recognized for its growing healthcare and biotechnology communities, its thriving cultural scene, and as a vibrant food hub. Job Description: Reporting to the Head of Collections and Systems, the Electronic Acquisitions Librarian is responsible for managing the acquisition, access, and ongoing maintenance of the library's electronic resources and related systems. This position oversees workflows associated with the electronic resource lifecycle, including purchasing, activation, access management, troubleshooting, and assessment. The Electronic Acquisitions Librarian collaborates closely with colleagues across the Collections Unit and throughout the library to ensure efficient acquisitions processes, timely invoice payment, reliable access to electronic collections, and effective stewardship of electronic resources. Major Responsibilities: Coordinates and manages the acquisition of electronic resources. Manages annual serials renewals through EBSCONET and works directly with vendors to ensure continuity of access and service. Assists with annual reviews of journal usage data to assess collection effectiveness and alignment with community needs. Assists with monograph purchase and provides timely communication to requestors regarding purchasing decisions. Collaborates with the Head of Collections and Systems to maintain and update knowledge bases, authentication systems (EZproxy), and discovery services as needed. Troubleshoots access issues related to electronic resources by identifying root causes, coordinating with vendors to resolve problems, and communicating status updates to users. Ensures that electronic resource holdings, entitlements, and coverage data are accurately maintained across library systems to facilitate reliable and seamless access. Collaborates with the Collections Team and other library staff on acquisitions initiatives, collection policies, vendor evaluations, and database selection. Coordinates reserve material ordering in support of teaching and learning needs. Supervises student employee(s) assigned to acquisitions and collections-related work. Coordinates the purchase of faculty-authored monographs for both Goddard Library and Special Collections. Maintains accurate acquisitions records and prepares reports to support collection assessment and budget management. Requirements: Master's degree from an ALA-accredited program. Minimum of two years of experience in the acquisition, management, and maintenance of electronic resources. Knowledge of the electronic resource lifecycle, including acquisition, licensing, access management, and ongoing maintenance. Familiarity with library metadata standards and practices, including MARC21, Dublin Core, and RDA. Knowledge of accounting principles related to library acquisitions, including fund accounting. Familiarity with current electronic resource standards, best practices, and protocols, including KBART, COUNTER, and SUSHI. Excellent organizational and time-management skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines. Strong analytical, written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Demonstrated attention to detail and commitment to accuracy. Commitment to maintaining current knowledge of developments in acquisitions, electronic resource management, scholarly communications, and publishing trends. Preferred Qualifications: Previous supervisory experience and experience working in an academic library environment, preferably in technical services. Experience collecting, managing, analyzing, and reporting acquisitions and collection data to support assessment and decision-making. Proficiency with an integrated library system, particularly acquisitions and electronic resource management modules; experience with OCLC WorldShare Management Services (WMS) strongly preferred or similar cloud-based ILS. Experience using bibliographic utilities and cataloging tools, such as OCLC Connexion. Experience selecting, ordering, and managing library materials using online acquisitions platforms such as GOBI. Demonstrated technical aptitude and troubleshooting skills, with the ability to work independently and collaboratively in a team environment. Additional Information: Expected Hiring Range: $51,700 to $68,150 Pay Transparency Disclosure: The compensation for this position will be determined based on factors that include available budget, internal equity, and the selected candidate's qualifications, experience, education, and other job-related credentials. This range represents Clark University's good-faith estimate of the expected hiring range at the time of posting consistent with Clark's compensation philosophy and internal alignment. At Clark University we believe that diversity of experiences, perspectives, and backgrounds leads to a more innovative and productive work environment. We welcome and encourage individuals of all backgrounds to join our team and contribute their unique ideas to help us achieve our goals. Clark University offers a generous benefit package for full and, if applicable, part-time employees that include; paid time off, generous retirement plan, group health and dental insurance, life insurance, and tuition, along with use of many campus amenities. For a complete list of benefits for eligible employees visit here . To review the Clark University Police Department Annual Security and Fire Safety Report visit here . Application Instructions: To be considered for this position, you must submit your credentials online. Create a Clark University Careers Account by clicking on the APPLY NOW button below. You will be able to upload the following documents, which are required for consideration: Resume/CV Cover letter See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Already have a Clark University Careers Account? Login to your account to add documents or update your account. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Salary will be commensurate with skills and experience. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States for any employer. Clark University participates in E-Verify to confirm employment eligibility in the United States. A successful background check is required upon acceptance. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Clark University 950 Main Street Worcester, MA 01610"
